WEBVTT

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.710
Hao De.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:10.510
"Wa"

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:10.510
Yes?

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.800
Behind you.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.430
Tch!

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.510
Wha--

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:18.720
What's <i>that</i>?!

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.020
Eh?

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.180
Enemies? From behind?!

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.950
That's Lu Wuwei and Gan Yang!

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:38.780
Didn't you tell me they'd
been <i>slain</i>, Ba Miu?

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.660
Th-They really scattered at the end
there--I totally thought they were dead!

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.580
I rather suspected this would be the case.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.340
"Qin"

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.340
It--It's Commander Lu Wuwei!

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.340
And Commander Gan Yang, too!

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:56.220
Their small unit has launched a charge
at the Wa Lin Army's back!

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.180
Lu Wuwei... Gan Yang...

00:00:58.180 --> 00:00:59.760
So they're alive!

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.230
They're tenacious, all right.

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.770
What do you think, Bai Li?
Should we cover them, too?

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:12.900
It's no use--they're already right
on top of Wa Lin's army.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.320
Captain! Enemy attack from the left!

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:18.740
What?!

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.950
I-Isn't that--

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:27.500
They rode right on through!

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.630
We're not the ones they're after!

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.920
No--

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.840
They're going for the
Wa Lin Army's back, too!

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.340
Fear the Yu Feng Force!

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.640
Er... Wa Lin, ma'am?

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.720
Another new bunch of enemies
is coming up behind--

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.810
Hmm...

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:53.440
So many big-name foes, and all eyes on me.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.190
--Ba Miu!
--Ma'am?

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:57.030
We're moving.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:00.910
I've shown this spot enough
opulence and cuteness.

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:01.780
Eh?

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.330
Are... are we withdrawing for now?

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.160
Oh, no.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.880
"Meng"

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.880
We're going somewhere more <i>entertaining</i>.

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.390
"The Strongest"

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.390
In the Meng Wu/Han Ming battle
that began with an echelon sweep,

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.390
In the Meng Wu/Han Ming battle
that began with an echelon sweep,

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:49.310
Meng Wu's army launched a second
wave with 15,000 troops.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.190
Compared to the first wave,

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:59.860
the second concentrated manpower
on the left and right edges.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.780
"Bei Man"

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.780
Looking to crush us on both ends, eh?

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.240
"Gang Mozhu"

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:10.000
Han Ming's two aides each
commanded 10,000 men

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.790
where the two armies clashed.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.080
Stay strong! Push on in!

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:19.170
"Qin" "Meng"

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:19.170
Soon only Meng Wu's 5,000
remained behind them.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:22.470
Break through here and get to the inside!

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.390
Meng Wu's army was
putting on a fine fight,

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:28.720
but their momentum came to a complete halt

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:32.020
before Bei Man's and
Gang Mozhu's mighty army.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:35.730
Send the archers outside to
rain down arrows behind us.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:39.400
My heavy unit can handle a melee.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.400
Sir!

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:43.780
Damn.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:46.570
Our strength is sapped...

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:49.700
"Han"

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:49.700
Meng Wu is running out of options.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.620
Indeed.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:55.250
What he presented as
an all-out echelon attack

00:04:55.250 --> 00:05:00.630
was really a two-pronged tactic
focusing might on both ends.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:03.840
Unconventional, yes, but with
his manpower divided in two,

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.840
there's no going back
in the event of failure.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:11.350
And <i>this </i>is a complete
and utter tactical failure.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:15.140
So it goes when you're besotted
with unpracticed schemes.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.400
The fool.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.780
B-Begging your pardon! A word of advice?

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.530
Pass.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:25.150
Sir...

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:27.950
It's all according to plan...

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.370
<i>His </i>plan.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.290
An echelon sweep?

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:33.620
Yes.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:37.960
Surely you know I'm
not fond of cheap tricks.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:39.420
Of course.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:43.670
But this really does call
for some sort of scheme.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:46.630
Is the Chu army really
so formidable a foe?

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:49.800
Yes. And I say this as
a son of Chu myself.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:51.310
There is no doubt.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:55.350
So?

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:57.100
What <i>is </i>this tactic of yours?

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:01.770
The massive nation of Chu
puts much importance on honor.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:04.030
Han Ming is sure to meet
you head-on, confidently,

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.450
his troops in a line abreast.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:10.910
That's when you execute an
echelon sweep of 20,000 men.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:14.580
The enemy will likely send
reinforcements to the right.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:17.870
Then a second echelon sweep--with 15,000.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:21.920
Be sure to bulk up either end with troops.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:25.800
And strike with 35,000 of my 40 total?

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.430
That's the crucial part.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.840
The enemy will surmise
that the second sweep

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:34.470
is meant to destroy their
weak points at both ends.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:39.900
They'll divert their troops
far to the left and right.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:49.360
I see it now--

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.370
the path to Han Ming.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:57.200
This is the only way to strike Han Ming,
who's planted solidly in the back.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:01.000
Even then, this tactic can
only accomplish so much.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.920
The rest is up to you, Meng Wu.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:07.050
This is plenty.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:09.380
I know I've kept you waiting, men!

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:14.390
You are as hotblooded as I, but your turn

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:16.720
has come at the very last!

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.730
Know that your silence has all been

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:22.770
in service of this very moment!

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.230
All troops!

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:25.520
Charge!

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:29.860
It's Meng Wu!

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:33.160
He's coming at us head-on,
his last 5,000 in tow!

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.950
Going out in a blaze of glory, is he?

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:42.290
If he's coming after us, he's relied
too much on military force!

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:45.670
One can hardly call that a <i>plan</i>.

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:49.090
Bring the rear reinforcements around!

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:52.260
If he had any assurance that those 5,000

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:55.430
can best the 10,000 in my main camp,

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:58.140
then his plan is a fine one, indeed.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:03.270
But are you <i>really </i>that strong, Meng Wu?

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.190
Let's just see your might!

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:09.650
Bring out the 5,000 in the
Savage Giants mounted unit!

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:17.370
My main camp is more
than just these 10,000!

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.490
Outta my way! Move!

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:21.330
Th-They're <i>massive</i>!

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.170
There's cavalry over there!

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:26.960
Tch!

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:30.710
Those horsemen... they look big.

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.630
It... It can't be!

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.640
Are <i>all </i>of them as huge as Meng Wu?!

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:52.570
My goodness! He sent the giants flying!

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.660
Follow Meng Wu!

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:02.330
With this strategy, Meng Wu,
there's no going back.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:04.870
You'll use every last one
of your 40,000 troops

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:08.750
as you make your way
to the enemy's main camp.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.090
Failure is not an option.

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:13.630
Release the power within
in a grand explosion!

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:19.430
No matter what, this single blow

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:22.180
must slay Chu's commanding general,

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:26.140
the very symbol of the
coalition army's power!

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.900
Han Ming!

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:32.530
All right! We're through!

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:36.910
Huh?

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:38.990
It's... it's Meng Wu!

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:41.080
He's finally joined the fray!

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.040
Clear a path!

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.660
This is no time to loll around!

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.000
After Meng Wu!

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:53.340
Han Ming, sir! Meng Wu approaches!

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:59.300
Oh, my goodness me. You don't say.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:02.430
So Meng Wu's come out to play.

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:05.020
We're a little off course.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:08.850
Changing bearing slightly to the left!

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:12.320
We should pick up the pace, Wa Lin, ma'am.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:17.150
It would seem Meng Wu is
on track to reach Han Ming.

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:20.570
No, this is just fine.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:24.240
One needn't be early
for <i>everything</i>, you know.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:28.960
Meng Tian, sir!

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:32.840
Wa Lin is headed to Meng Wu's
battlefield, beside us!

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.550
Chu general Wa Lin.

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:37.510
I can't tell what she might be thinking.

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:41.010
Does she mean to slay my father, Meng Wu?

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:44.350
But she only has her main army of 5,000--

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:47.640
the remaining 50,000 are here.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:51.610
Which is why General Teng can't get away.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:54.860
Ditto for Lu Wuwei and Gan Yang.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:57.150
Still, someone needs to follow Wa Lin.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:02.490
The Yu Feng Force!

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:04.330
Wang Ben...

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:06.910
Great minds think alike, eh?

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.080
Lu Xian!

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:11.170
I'm putting you in charge
of the cavalry here.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:13.380
I need 700 horsemen! Come with me!

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.420
You're leaving?

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:19.170
Yeah. Wa Lin probably has
her eye on Meng Wu.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:21.300
If the neighboring battlefield goes down,

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:24.680
Han Ming's troops will come here next.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:26.350
Besides...

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:29.430
My little brother'll
be sad if Father dies.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:35.230
Fill Pops in, too, will you? Thanks!

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.070
Meng Tian...

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:38.320
Bai Li!

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:41.030
General Wa Lin has up and left!

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:44.200
What should we do?

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.160
No one else is moving.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:49.200
We'll just keep on fighting where we are!

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:53.580
What on earth is going through
General Wa Lin's mind?

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:58.380
Did that elite unit of 5,000
really go off to kill Meng Wu?

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:01.430
Wait--5,000?

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:04.390
But Wa Lin's elites number 10,000.

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.600
What of the other five?

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:07.760
Stop them!

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:08.930
Here they come!

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:12.560
Next stop: the main camp!

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.690
Who's the strongest?

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:21.530
Who's the strongest?

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:23.490
Who's the strongest?

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:25.280
Han Ming!

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:28.490
What the hell?

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.000
Who's the strongest?

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.670
Who's the strongest?

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.750
Who's the strongest?

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:38.880
Han Ming!

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:41.760
He shatters great boulders at a breath!

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:45.010
He flattens mountains into the
earth with a single swing!

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:48.890
The world's strongest--a man among men!

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:49.850
Tch!

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:52.890
Who is he?

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.520
Han Ming!

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.520
You finally showed up.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:09.280
What a coincidence.

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:12.000
I, too, pride myself on being the
strongest in the Middle Kingdom.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:18.380
If you make that claim, too,
then we must settle this:

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:20.920
Which of us is the <i>real </i>man?

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:33.230
At last...

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:34.270
He's here!

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:38.480
You're chattier than I thought.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:41.360
It's obvious which of us is the real deal.

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:43.240
Now bring it on.

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:47.870
I'll beat that crab-head
of yours into a pulp.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:50.200
Shut your mouth, peon.

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:58.790
Using my sword against your
weapon would likely nick its blade.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:04.130
It's been ten years.

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:08.220
Ten years since a foe has
made me hoist the mace.

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:12.430
Th-This is it: Meng Wu and Han Ming!

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:15.230
He's finally managed to draw him out!

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:18.310
Not only is Han Ming
a great general of Chu,

00:14:18.310 --> 00:14:21.770
he represents the might of
the whole coalition army.

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:23.480
If Han Ming is slain,

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:27.530
it will affect every battlefield--
tactically and otherwise.

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:38.330
Whoa!

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:44.840
Meng Wu, sir!

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.800
Ha! How'd you like that?

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:51.350
Didn't expect you to be such a pushover,

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:53.510
Meng Wu.

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:54.520
Tch.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:59.100
Han Ming!

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.310
--Only two swings,

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:01.480
--Han Ming!
--Only two swings,

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:03.230
--and Meng Wu is thoroughly defeated!

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:05.280
--Han Ming!
--and Meng Wu is thoroughly defeated!

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:11.780
--Han Ming is Meng Wu's superior
in both physique <i>and </i>armed force.
--Han Ming!

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:14.620
Don't lose heart, now.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:18.330
It's not like you disappointed me.

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:21.540
No, there's no disappointing Han Ming.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:25.630
I already <i>know </i>I'm
the strongest man alive.

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:31.220
I am no longer discouraged knowing
that no foe can stir my blood.

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:35.010
I never had a foe--
not from the very beginning.

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:39.600
Not even once, starting from
my first campaign.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:44.230
I came from the east,
tearing up front lines as I went.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:49.110
I fought Qi, Zhao, Wei, Han.

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:54.280
I must have conquered about
a hundred castles in my long career.

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:57.370
In that whole time, I never lost once.

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:59.500
Not even <i>once</i>.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.830
On those four nations' front lines,

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:06.920
the mere mention of the terrifying name
Han Ming made men soil their pants.

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:12.430
I remain relatively unknown only
in the distant land of Yan...

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.850
and in your Qin.

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:19.730
Ah, because Qin and Chu haven't
fought these last 20, 30 years?

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:22.100
You may think so,

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:25.440
but that is not the reason.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:26.940
There was once--<i>once</i>--

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:31.400
a fool who came south
looking to snatch up Chu.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:36.120
A great general at the time--indeed,
lauded as one of your Six Greats:

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:37.740
Wang He!

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:38.740
Wha--

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:41.290
What?!

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:42.790
Yan Bu!

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:44.750
He... he's lying.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.420
I've been on the front lines
ever since that era,

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:50.090
but I never heard anything like that!

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:53.550
It's no lie.

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:59.260
I was an unstoppable young general
at the height of my power.

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:01.480
I was specifically selected,

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:05.600
as adjutant to the great General
Xian Yan, the Tiger of Chu,

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:08.230
to intercept this fellow.

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:13.400
And then...

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:20.450
I defeated Wang He handily
with my first charge.

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:26.040
Back to Qin territory he crawled,
gravely wounded.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:29.630
You can guess why that battle
is not well known in Qin

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:34.090
by simply considering how
thoroughly Wang He lost.

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:36.130
That's... That's bullshit!

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:38.800
One of the Six Greats,
losing like that to Chu?!

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.720
Actually...

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:46.230
I <i>have </i>heard there's a lost battle with
Chu that's forbidden to speak of.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:52.570
But even besting a great general
like Wang He didn't lift my spirits.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:55.820
I had come to the realization long ago:

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.820
By some quirk of heaven,

00:17:57.820 --> 00:18:02.040
I, Han Ming, was born
surpassing the limits of man!

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.250
I am <i>transcendent</i>!

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:08.880
Meng Wu!

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:12.050
Here's something interesting:

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:14.720
What might a peerless being like me

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:18.180
think of fighting on the battlefield?

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:20.760
Only one word comes to mind:

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:23.680
"Boring."

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.390
Then why do I fight at all?

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:29.650
In search of a genuine foe?

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:31.480
No!

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:33.570
It's my <i>duty</i>!

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:36.700
I face those who mistakenly
think they're mighty

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:39.870
and crush them head-on!

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:47.000
I fulfill my duty as a transcendent man,
a great general from a truly great land!

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:48.960
And <i>that</i>

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.880
is Han Ming, Giant of Chu!

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:55.210
Han Ming!

00:18:57.340 --> 00:18:58.680
Han Ming!

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:02.180
Han Ming!

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:09.520
M-Meng Wu, sir!

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:13.650
There's no way he can beat Han Ming.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.400
It's all over--for Meng Wu

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:18.400
and for Qin.

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:33.170
Th-That's absurd...

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:35.380
<i>The </i>Han Ming...

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:37.050
...sent flying?!

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:41.640
Boring, you say?

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:43.470
I'm the opposite.

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:45.140
Han Ming.

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:49.770
Never before have I fought
someone as mighty as you.

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:53.270
And so, I am exhilarated!

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:55.730
Not because I've found a worthy opponent

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:58.280
or out of any sense of sentimentality.

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:00.450
No, I am happy because,

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:01.860
at long last,

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:04.950
for the first time in my life,

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:08.750
the time has come for me
to fight with <i>all </i>my might!

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:11.790
Han Ming!

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:15.290
You're not transcendent.

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:16.960
No...

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:21.130
You've just been damned lucky
with your opponents--until today!

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:23.970
Shut up, little man.

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:25.800
"Han Ming"
"Meng Wu"

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:28.180
"Bei Man"
"Lai Hui"
"Ding Zhi"

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:31.390
Lai Hui, sir! Fall back!

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:32.940
The enemy's sheer momentum--!

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:36.610
Are you crazy?
We're not leaving this spot!

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:39.900
This is how our lord can battle Han Ming--

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:42.320
while we're keeping
the enemy's men occupied!

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:44.740
But we can't hold out any longer!

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:47.280
Lai Hui, sir, you might perish!

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:49.080
I don't care if I die!

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:52.540
That's just how important this is--

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.250
this battle of ours!

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:05.300
Meng--

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:08.850
The sound... Is this a <i>human </i>battle?

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:14.310
Sh-Shrapnel!

00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:15.730
Pull back a little!

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:24.950
Meng Wu, sir!

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:31.450
Th-This is ridiculous! What <i>is </i>that man?!

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:35.710
To think anyone could hold his own
like this against Han Ming!

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:40.300
Meng Wu... he's strong, all right.

00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:44.510
More than twice as strong as
our intel had led us to believe.

00:21:44.510 --> 00:21:48.390
Another monster, of a sort.

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:53.100
"Chu"

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:53.100
Given his build and his
natural-born talent for battle,

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:55.980
he may well be on a par with Han Ming.

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:57.810
No!

00:21:57.810 --> 00:21:59.820
Then tell me, Ren Ao:

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:03.360
Is it possible that Han Ming may... lose?

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:07.320
Not a chance in hell!

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:09.910
A duel between two great generals

00:22:09.910 --> 00:22:13.910
is not simply a clash of force.

00:22:13.910 --> 00:22:17.330
They fight with the strength of the
ranks they've earned as generals

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:20.630
resting on their shoulders.

00:22:20.630 --> 00:22:23.920
As a tactician, I can't say I understand--

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:27.220
but such things do exist!

00:22:27.220 --> 00:22:31.390
The wartime careers of
Han Ming and Meng Wu

00:22:31.390 --> 00:22:34.060
are like night and day.

00:22:34.060 --> 00:22:36.270
On Han Ming's shoulders

00:22:36.270 --> 00:22:40.770
rests the might of a great
Middle Kingdom general.

00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:42.650
Though his battle prowess may be similar,

00:22:42.650 --> 00:22:46.950
Meng Wu will <i>never </i>defeat
Han Ming in a duel!

00:23:04.130 --> 00:23:07.420
Meng Wu!

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:14.930
It's over.

00:24:54.280 --> 00:24:58.490
Next on <i>Kingdom</i>: "The Mightiest Man."
